---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Claims Desk"
  description="A substantiation registry for product claims. Case study forthcoming."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1 max-w-3xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-medium">Claims Desk</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      Claims Desk is a substantiation registry: product claims go in, an
      adversarial review loop runs against the available evidence, and what comes
      out is a public ruling anyone can fetch. The full case study is still being
      written.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      In the meantime, there is a working demonstration — a product page whose
      every claim is anchored, listed in a machine-readable manifest, and linked
      to its substantiation record in the registry.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6">
      <a
        href="/projects/claims-desk/demo"
        class="text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 underline underline-offset-4"
      >
        See the claims manifest demo
      </a>
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
